    {
      "id": "claim_640c9edaf6d34d1683bb9dc1e1560adc",
      "statement": "Parse verifies the token signature with a key while ParseInsecure deliberately uses UnsafeClaimsWithoutVerification; CA flows use ParseInsecure because the CLI only inspects claims (e.g. the sha claim) before sending the token to the CA which verifies it. AWS tokens get their instance identity document unmarshaled and Azure tokens get xms_mirid parsed into subscription/resource-group/name components.",
      "evidence": [
