    {
      "id": "claim_3d700818af314e7a8bb708f76c5cd7e7",
      "statement": "Per-provisioner generation: X5C signs with the certificate key (file or KMS via cryptoutil.CreateSigner) embedding the chain in x5c or x5cAllowInvalid headers; Nebula uses the nebula header; SSHPOP is restricted to SSH revoke/renew/rekey types; K8sSA reads the pod service-account token file; GCP/AWS/Azure call the provisioner's own GetIdentityToken (possibly setting DisableCustomSANs); ACME and SCEP return ACMETokenError/SCEPTokenError so callers reroute to their own flows.",
